# UST.G3AE: Second-H First-Order Joint Graph/Coefficient Lift Theorem

## Status

`CLOSED_EXACT_FINITE_RING_FIRST_ORDER_CONSTRUCTIVE_LIFT`

`UST.G3AD` proves that the independently chosen smooth integer-`gamma`
coefficient lift does not contain the selected second primitive-`H` graph.
This theorem answers the immediate follow-up:

> Is that nonzero row an obstruction to the graph-Prym family, or only to the
> independently chosen coefficient lift?

At first `101`-adic order it is only an obstruction to the fixed lift. The
coefficient vector can be deformed together with the graph so that containment
is restored exactly modulo `101^2`.

